# --- generated / regenerable artifacts (do not commit; rebuild via scripts) ---
# Entire assets/ tree is local/HF (runs, seeds, Phoenix DBs, etc.) — never git.
# datasets/ stays at the repo root.
#
# NOTE the `assets/*` (not `assets/`) form: an excluded DIRECTORY can never have its
# contents re-included, so the tree has to be excluded entry-by-entry for the deck
# exception below to be reachable at all.
assets/*
datasets/

# EXCEPTION — the easy__google-slides__001 seed deck.
# Every other file under assets/ is regenerable or mirrored to HF, but this one is a
# ground-truth fixture that NOTHING regenerates, so it has to be version-controlled.
# Leaving it uncommitted is precisely how it silently rotted: two files both named
# "Q3 Review" existed, the device kept the 1-slide one, and six runs in Aug/Sep 2026
# self-reported a PASS against it. Git's negation rules require each parent to be
# re-included, hence the alternating pair of lines.
!assets/seeds
assets/seeds/*
!assets/seeds/public
assets/seeds/public/*
!assets/seeds/public/Q3_Review.pptx

# EXCEPTION — the hard__drive-notes-telegram__010 seed note.
# Same reasoning as the deck above, and the same failure mode: the OnePlus Notes app
# keeps the note in app-private storage with no file seed, so nothing could recreate it
# once a run had edited or the app had lost it. Its text is now version-controlled here
# and reset_phone.py re-types it whenever the note drifts, verifying the result against
# `com.oneplus.note:id/text_count` (whitespace-excluded), which is 518 for this text.
!assets/seeds/public/Budget Deadline (OnePlus Notes).txt

